hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2820","Narrated to us ‘Ali ibn al-Hujjaj al-Sa’di, he said: Hushaim informed us, he said: Isma’il ibn Abi Khalid and Zakariyya ibn Abi Za’ida informed us.\n\nAnd narrated to us ‘Ali as well, he said: ‘Ali ibn Mus-hir and Sa’dan—meaning Ibn Yahya—informed us from Isma’il.\n\nAnd narrated to us Muhammad ibn ‘Abd al-A’la al-Sana’ani, he said: al-Mu’tamir informed us, he said: I heard Isma’il.\n\nAnd narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, he said: Yahya and Yazid ibn Harun informed us. Yahya said: Isma’il narrated to us. And Yazid said: Isma’il informed us.\n\nAnd narrated to us ‘Ali ibn al-Mundhir, he said: Ibn Fudayl informed us, he said: Isma’il informed us.\n\nAnd narrated to us ‘Abd Allah ibn Sa’id al-Ashajj and Salam ibn Junada, they both said: Waki’ informed us from Isma’il ibn Abi Khalid.\n\nThis is the hadith of Hushaim from al-Sha’bi, who said: ‘Urwa ibn Mudarris ibn Aus ibn Haritha ibn Lam al-Ta’i informed me, he said: I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) while he was at al-Jam’ (al-Muzdalifah), so I said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have come to you from the mountain of Tayy’; I have exhausted my mount and wearied my soul. By Allah, I have not left any pass without halting at it. Do I have any Hajj (i.e., is it valid)?”\n\nSo the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever prays this prayer with us and stands with us at this standing (i.e., at al-Muzdalifah), and then departs before that from ‘Arafat by night or by day, then his Hajj is complete and he has removed his impurities (i.e., the rites of Hajj are fulfilled).”\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
